    Spotlight
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2
    style="
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin-top: 2px !important;
      margin: 0;
    "
  >
    $2B war damage
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    <mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  target="_blank"
/>
    
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What happened? </strong>The US has lost <a href="https://www.trtworld.com/article/35eac28b7995" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">nearly $2B worth of military equipment</a> amid its attacks against Iran since Saturday. The most significant loss was a $1.1B early-warning radar at Al Udeid Air Base in Qatar. Other damage included satellite terminals in Bahrain, a THAAD radar in the UAE, and three F-15E jets lost over Kuwait, as strikes also hit US bases and diplomatic sites. <br><br><strong>On the ground:</strong> Iran launched waves of missiles and drones toward Israel as the <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/israel-iran-continue-attacks-as-war-enters-its-fifth-day-engulfs-region" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">US-Israel war with Iran entered its fifth day</a>. Iranian forces targeted a consulate in Dubai, a CIA station in Saudi Arabia, and a US base in Qatar. Meanwhile, Israel carried out airstrikes across Tehran and other Iranian cities targeting military and security facilities.  At least 787 people have been killed across Iran in joint US-Israeli attacks.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Meanwhile:</strong> Spain has said the <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/2/spain-refuses-to-let-us-use-bases-for-iran-attacks" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">US is not using its joint military bases on Spanish territory</a> for operations against Iran and that Madrid will not authorize their use for such attacks. PM Pedro Sánchez condemned the US-Israeli strikes on Iran as unjustified and dangerous. While Spain has also criticised Iran’s retaliatory attacks in the Gulf, its refusal to support military operations from its bases sets it apart from several European allies that have backed US actions.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
