<mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 0.5px 1px 1px" border-radius="5px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="5px" padding="0px">
    
    <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2
    style="
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      font-weight: 500;
      margin-top: 2px !important;
      margin: 0;
    "
  >
    China’s next phase
  </h2>
</mj-text>
    
    
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Summary: China unveils five-year plan focusing on tech self-reliance, consumption growth, and drones.</strong></p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>What’s happening? </strong>China will unveil its <a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/china-set-to-release-new-five-year-plan-at-national-peoples-congress" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">15th Five-Year Plan</a> (2026-2030) during the National People’s Congress (NPC) in Beijing. The plan is expected to focus on industrial self-reliance, technological innovation, renewable energy, and consumption-led growth. It will also address challenges such as the US trade war, slowing domestic demand, and weak consumer confidence. Premier Li Qiang will present China’s annual work report and might set economic growth targets around 5%.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Low altitude economy:</strong> This will be one of the key concepts discussed at the NPC. China’s “low-altitude economy” refers to the development and commercial use of airspace below about 1,000 meters to support logistics systems. The strategy focuses on technologies such as delivery drones, electric vertical take-off and landing (eVTOL) aircraft, aerial taxis, agricultural drones, and surveillance or inspection systems. Regulators are expected to introduce updated airspace management rules, infrastructure, and safety standards at the NPC.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Big picture:</strong> Chinese officials face the difficult task of shifting the economy toward consumption-led growth. Economists expect policies to boost domestic demand, expand services, and reduce urban-rural wage gaps. A proposed “Law on Promoting Ethnic Unity and Progress” seeks to strengthen a shared national identity across China’s 56 ethnic groups, potentially increasing cultural and political assimilation.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="10px" />
    </mj-section>
    <mj-spacer height="10px" />
    <mj-section
