        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇳🇵 Nepal - Ready for election. </strong>Nepal is heading to a general election on 5 March, its first national vote since youth-led protests last September. Nearly 19Mn voters will choose a 275-member parliament, with 165 lawmakers elected directly and 110 through proportional representation. Traditional parties such as the Nepali Congress and Communist Party of Nepal (Unified Marxist-Leninist) face a challenge from the newer Rastriya Swatantra Party led by reformist candidate Balendra Shah (<a href="https://www.tbsnews.net/world/nepal-vote-first-election-gen-z-led-protests-toppled-government-1376766" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">scripting the future</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇪🇨 Ecuador - Operation against drugs.</strong> Ecuador and the US have launched joint military operations targeting drug-trafficking groups that authorities describe as “narco-terrorist” organizations. They aim to disrupt cocaine trafficking networks operating through Ecuador’s ports and territory. Ecuadorian forces are carrying out the ground operations, while US personnel provide planning, intelligence, and logistical support (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgjzz4gn64zo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">no to drugs</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇳🇴 Norway - Additional charges. </strong>Prosecutors in Norway have filed additional charges against Marius Borg Høiby, the son of Crown Princess Mette-Marit. The 29-year-old faces 40 charges, including rape, reckless behaviour, and violating a restraining order. Høiby denies some of the allegations, particularly four rape counts involving a woman allegedly asleep or incapacitated. Prosecutors say he has admitted some offences (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0e5r28y3xqo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">more drama</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇬🇧 UK - Visa restrictions</strong>. ⁠The UK said it will end study visas for students from Afghanistan, Cameroon, Myanmar, and Sudan, and work visas for Afghans. The Home Office said applications from these groups increased by more than 470% between 2021 and 2025. Officials described the measure as an “emergency brake” to prevent misuse of the visa system while maintaining protection for genuine refugees (<a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/4/uk-to-end-study-visas-for-myanmar-afghanistan-cameroon-sudan-students" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">recalibration</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇺🇲 US - War insurance.</strong> President Trump announced that the US government will provide political risk insurance for ships traveling through the Gulf. The insurance will be offered through the United States International Development Finance Corporation to help shipping companies continue operating despite rising security risks. Trump also said the United States Navy may escort oil tankers through the strait if necessary (<a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/3/us-will-provide-insurance-for-ships-in-gulf-amid-iranian-attacks-trump" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">US assures</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
